{"name":"Grenadine Pink","hex":"#ff616b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grenadine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cordial syrup made from pomegranates.","A dilute drink made from this syrup."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A syrup made from cloves and other spices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grenadine"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grenadine","blocks":[{"text":"Grenadine is a nonalcoholic bar syrup commonly used as a cocktail ingredient, distinguished by its sweetness, mild flavor, and red color. Popular in mixed drinks, grenadine syrup was traditionally made from pomegranate, but today is most commonly made from commercially produced natural or artificial flavors, as well as substitute fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Grenadinesyrup.jpg/330px-Grenadinesyrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grenadine","wikidata":"Q1136498"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/